 "title": "Lake County Assessor – Lake County, MN",
 "text": "Lake County Assessor – Lake County, MN\nSkip to content\nSkip to left sidebar\nSkip to footer\nHome\nDepartments\nAssessor\nAttorney\nAuditor\nCourt Administration\nEmergency Management\nEnvironmental Services\nPlanning and Zoning\nSolid Waste\nFacilities\nForestry\nGeographic Information Systems\nHealth and Human Services\nHighway\nHuman Resources\nCurrent Job Postings\nNorth Shore Collaborative\nRecorder\nSheriff\nSoil and Water Conservation District\nUniversity of MN Extension – 4-H\nVeterans Services\nVital Records\nCounty Board\nCalendar\nDocument Center\nSupport Guide\nAdults and Aging\nChemical Dependency and Addiction\nChild Care Providers\nChildren and Families\nClothing and Household\nDental\nDisability and Adaptive Services\nDomestic Violence and Sexual Assault\nEducation\nEmergency and Law Enforcement\nEmployment\nFinancial\nFood\nGovernment and General\nHealth and Wellness\nHousing\nLegal\nMental Health\nTransportation\nVeteran Services\nMenu\nHome\nDepartments\nAssessor\nAttorney\nAuditor\nCourt Administration\nEmergency Management\nEnvironmental Services\nPlanning and Zoning\nSolid Waste\nFacilities\nForestry\nGeographic Information Systems\nHealth and Human Services\nHighway\nHuman Resources\nCurrent Job Postings\nNorth Shore Collaborative\nRecorder\nSheriff\nSoil and Water Conservation District\nUniversity of MN Extension – 4-H\nVeterans Services\nVital Records\nCounty Board\nCalendar\nDocument Center\nSupport Guide\nAdults and Aging\nChemical Dependency and Addiction\nChild Care Providers\nChildren and Families\nClothing and Household\nDental\nDisability and Adaptive Services\nDomestic Violence and Sexual Assault\nEducation\nEmergency and Law Enforcement\nEmployment\nFinancial\nFood\nGovernment and General\nHealth and Wellness\nHousing\nLegal\nMental Health\nTransportation\nVeteran Services\nSearch:\nLake County Assessor\nThe Assessor’s Department provides for the equitable assessment of real and personal property in Lake County as provided by state law and regulation. It determines the value of all County property and makes the assessment based upon appraisals done by the appraiser staff and/or local assessors.\nPlease keep in mind that we have records for Lake County property only. We cannot access the records from neighboring counties.\nThe Assessor’s Office also reviews and corrects local assessment books, prepares abstracts, maps and other forms prescribed by the State Commissioner of Revenue, attends local and state Board of Equalization meetings, and appears in court to defend assessments as an expert witness.\nSpecific functions include: physical inspection and valuation of property, collects and maintains sales data, conducts and evaluates assessment ratio studies, administers valuation appeals and advises municipalities and the county board on assessment issues.\nFront desk of Lake County Assessor’s office\nAssessor Home\nAssessor Staff\nWhat Does an Assessor Do?\nFrequently Asked Questions about Property Assessments\nAssessment Calendar\nAppeal Your Assessment\nLocal Board of Equalization\nHomestead Market Value Exclusion\nProperty Tax Refund\nProperty Tax Exemption\nAdditional Programs\nLinks\nLake County Tax Records\nMN Department of Revenue\nMN State Statutes\nMN Tax Court\nAssessor\n601 3rd Ave\nTwo Harbors, MN 55616\nPhone (218) 834-8310\nFax (218) 834-8302\nWeekdays – 8:00 AM to 4:30 PM\nWeekends – Closed\nHoliday Closures\n1-800-450-8832\nFacebook\nOpen Monday-Friday\nCourthouse and Law Enforcement Center | 8:00AM-4:30PM\nHealth and Human Services | 8:00AM-4:00PM\nHighway | 7:00AM-3:00PM\nHoliday Closures\nCounty Employee Login\nprevious next slideshow",
